Data availability

            CHELSA-W5E5 is available at https://chelsa-climate.org/. The GGCMI phase 3 crop calendar is available via Zenodo at https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5062513 (ref. 51). A dataset of wheat yield at a 4-km resolution during 1982–2020 (named GlobalWheatYield4km) is available via Figshare at https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.10025006 (ref. 61). The soil data that support the simulation with crop model (DSSAT) in this study are available at https://doi.org/10.7910/DVN/1PEEY0. Fertilizer inputs are available at https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.4954582 (ref. 46). GGCMI Phase 3 model outputs are available at https://data.isimip.org/search/query//tree/ISIMIP3a/OutputData/agriculture/. GGCMI phase 1 model outputs are available under open data license CC BY 4.0 at https://zenodo.org (see Online-only Table 4 in ref. 18). Subnational crop yield statistics are available at depositories listed in Supplementary Table 4. Irrigated and rainfed wheat harvested area is available at https://www.uni-frankfurt.de/45218031/Data_download_center_for_MIRCA2000. The Emergency Events Database is available at https://www.emdat.be/ (ref. 22). SPAM is available at https://doi.org/10.7910/DVN/PRFF8V (ref. 52). A dataset of crop yield at a 5-min resolution during 1982–2015 (named GlobalCropYield5min) is available at https://doi.org/10.17632/hg8wzgx4yp.3. GSWP3-W5E5 is available at https://data.isimip.org/search/simulation_round/ISIMIP3a/product/InputData/climate_forcing/gswp3-w5e5/. Wheat experimental data from agro-meteorological stations and corresponding weather data from meteorological stations are available at http://data.cma.cn. GLASS LAI dataset is available at https://glass-product.bnu.edu.cn/introduction/LAI.html. GIMMS LAI4g dataset is available via Zenodo at https://zenodo.org/records/8281930 (ref. 62). The GLOBMAP LAI dataset is available via Zenodo at https://zenodo.org/records/4700264 (ref. 63). Source data are provided with this paper.
          Code availability

            The codes for global gridded crop model calibration and EWE identification and impact assessment are available via Figshare at https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.30846617 (ref. 64).
